# scripts/windows.env — pinned mingw-w64 cross-compiler version for the
# Windows server target (server/host/windows/, docs/DESIGN.md §2.1/§6.4).
#
# The Windows test machine has no C toolchain at all (server/backends/
# vendor/README.md, server/host/windows/main.c's header) -- the host is
# cross-compiled from Linux with mingw-w64 and copied over. mingw-w64 is a
# HOST package, not a container image, exactly like the Android SDK/NDK
# (scripts/android.env) and unlike devkitARM/devkitA64/PSPDEV/VITASDK
# (scripts/toolchains.env) -- so there is no digest to pin here. This file
# plays scripts/android.env's role for the windows target: both
# scripts/build.sh windows and .github/workflows/ci.yml's server-windows
# job read it, and scripts/windows-mingw-check.sh checks what's actually
# installed against it.
#
# Unlike android.env's JDK/NDK/cmdline-tools -- each fetched from a pinned
# URL and verified by checksum -- mingw-w64 here is a normal Ubuntu apt
# package (gcc-mingw-w64-x86-64 / g++-mingw-w64-x86-64 /
# binutils-mingw-w64-x86-64), and nothing under scripts/ may run apt-get
# (no passwordless sudo is assumed). What is pinned below is the exact version this backend
# was last verified against; scripts/windows-mingw-check.sh WARNS, and does
# NOT fail, when the installed version differs. That is a deliberate
# difference from every digest-pinned target in this repo: `apt-get install
# pkg=version` is not reliably resolvable across Ubuntu releases/runner
# images the way a Docker digest is guaranteed to resolve, so a hard
# mismatch-fails check would break on a routine `ubuntu-latest` bump for a
# reason that has nothing to do with this project. CI's server-windows job
# installs whatever `ubuntu-latest` currently offers under these package
# names and reports the version it got; if that version ever produces a
# build that actually fails, THAT is the real failure and shows up as this
# job going red, not as a version-string mismatch.
#
# Verified 2026-08-10 on this dev machine: server/backends/vigem.c, the
# vendored ViGEmClient.cpp (via server/backends/vendor/mingw-compat/, see
# vendor/README.md for the two include traps and why -isystem is required),
# shim/net_winsock.c, shim/time_win32.c and server/host/windows/main.c all
# compile cleanly with this compiler under -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror
# -pedantic (the vendored .cpp is compiled separately, without -Werror --
# see scripts/build.sh's build_windows() for why), and
# `x86_64-w64-mingw32-g++ -static` links a dependency-free PE32+ binary:
# confirmed with `objdump -p` that a non-static link pulls in
# libgcc_s_seh-1.dll and libstdc++-6.dll (which the target Windows machine
# does not have -- docs/DESIGN.md §2.1), and that -static removes both, leaving
# only KERNEL32/msvcrt/WS2_32/SETUPAPI/IPHLPAPI, plus BCRYPT since the §10
# pairing work of 2026-08-10 -- all part of any stock Windows install.

APAD_MINGW_TRIPLE=x86_64-w64-mingw32

# `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc --version`'s first line, and the Debian/Ubuntu
# package version (`dpkg -s gcc-mingw-w64-x86-64`) that produced it, for
# whoever is trying to reproduce this exactly rather than just "some
# mingw-w64".
APAD_MINGW_GCC_VERSION="13-win32"
APAD_MINGW_PKG_VERSION="13.2.0-6ubuntu1+26.1"

# apt package names scripts/windows-mingw-check.sh reports and CI's
# server-windows job installs. binutils-mingw-w64-x86-64 is listed
# explicitly even though the gcc/g++ packages pull it in transitively, so
# the apt-get line is copy-pasteable on its own.
APAD_MINGW_PACKAGES="gcc-mingw-w64-x86-64 g++-mingw-w64-x86-64 binutils-mingw-w64-x86-64"

# Extra libraries the final -static link needs beyond libc/libstdc++
# (verified against server/backends/vigem.c + the vendored ViGEmClient.cpp
# + server/host/windows/main.c, see scripts/build.sh's build_windows()):
#   -lws2_32    Winsock (shim/net_winsock.c)
#   -lsetupapi  SetupDi* device enumeration (ViGEmClient.cpp, bus discovery)
#   -liphlpapi  GetAdaptersAddresses (server/host/windows/main.c, tier-3
#               "print my own IP" — docs/PROTOCOL.md §7)
#   -lbcrypt    BCryptGenRandom (server/host/windows/main.c, cfg.on_random —
#               the §10 pairing secret. CNG, in every supported Windows;
#               nothing in libapadserver reaches for entropy itself)
APAD_MINGW_LIBS="-lws2_32 -lsetupapi -liphlpapi -lbcrypt"
